    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0614" n="528" xml:id="pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.85/42: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Collier</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-30T15:00:00-04:42"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1927—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>115. Government has sent to Congress project of law embodying all points of my
                    111, August 25, 4 p.m., except point 2. Omission of latter will probably greatly
                    diminish opposition to bill by British shipowners and eliminate that of other
                    nations. Grace Line is seriously and almost solely threatened. I renew request
                    for instructions by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
